## Original Content
<p>In addition to data protection, the EU’s General Data Protection Regulation requires businesses to ensure consumers can exercise their data privacy rights. But first, individuals must know these rights.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://gdpr.eu/consumers-gdpr-data-privacy-rights/">Do consumers know their GDPR data privacy rights?</a> appeared first on <a href="https://gdpr.eu">GDPR.eu</a>.</p>

## Summary
The article discusses how the EU's General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) requires businesses to ensure consumers can exercise their data privacy rights, but emphasizes that consumer awareness of these rights is essential. It references a resource from GDPR.eu for further information on the topic.

## Key Points
- GDPR mandates that businesses facilitate consumers' exercise of data privacy rights.
- Consumer knowledge of their data privacy rights is a necessary prerequisite for exercising them.
- The article highlights the importance of consumer education in the context of data protection regulations.


